  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user, I want a darker dark mode, an OLED black option, 1 pt separators and a live preview in settings, so that the app suits my screen.\n\n### Scope\n\nColour tokens (#0B0B0C dark, OLED black), 1 pt separators, single accent, live preview in Settings. Overlaps named: compact mode stays in LOT-119 (#210) (not redone here); the one-line message header is a reader template change owned by LOT-106 (#197) (layout setting, on LOT-083's builder), this lot only supplies its tokens. Keep `[code]` monospace and user accent colours (Bybifok PR #5 blockers).\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: medium · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: FEAT-010 (#154)\n- Absorbs: FEAT-010 (part 1); legacy backlog P3 dark mode/contrast\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): Bybifok PR #5 (ideas only, not merged); `AppSettingsView.swift:422-468`\n- Spec: `docs/features/FEAT-010.md` (feature spec, ADR 0011 §2; write it first if absent, crediting Bybifok) plus a short `docs/lots/LOT-122-*.md` pointing to it\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-121 (#212, done)\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged\n\n### Feature umbrella\n\n- Implements FEAT-010 (#154), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: LOT-166 (#256); the last lot (LOT-166 (#256)) closes #154.\n\nFEAT issues (#145–#165) are umbrellas and are never claimed: claim this lot's issue; the PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #<FEAT issue>`.\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none known; any page state the spec needs and the fixtures lack is listed as *pending capture*, never hand-built (LESSONS 35-36)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Contrast ≥ 4.5:1 on text in every theme (measured).\n- [ ] No setting of LOT-119 (#210)/106 duplicated.\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
